  "description": "Shared vectors for the install-bound restore hash (backend-api.md section 4.3 step 1, ADR-012 Part B (d)). bodyHash = SHA-256(prefix || 0x00 || installId || 0x00 || JCS(body without attestation)). JCS is RFC 8785. Android: Play Integrity requestHash = b64u(bodyHash). iOS (R4-1(3)): seatKeysDigest = SHA-256(publicKey_0 || ... || publicKey_n-1), the raw 65-byte points of attestation.seatKeys in request order (SHA-256 of the empty string when seatKeys is absent), and the App Attest clientDataHash = SHA-256(clientDataPrefix || 0x00 || bodyHash || seatKeysDigest), used for both generateAssertion and attestKey. So attestation.seatKeys stays outside bodyHash (its jcs and bodyHash equal 'ios-member-order'), and each seat-key signature still signs challenge = bodyHash, but its public keys are covered by the App Attest assertion: a proxy can't add, drop, reorder or replace a key. The Dart (T-145) and .NET (T-132) implementations must reproduce every 'valid' vector exactly and reject every 'invalid' one with 400 VALIDATION_FAILED, at any nesting depth (the strict parse runs over the whole body, attestation included). All values are synthetic.",
